From: inFAMOUS FoB Recomp contributors
Subject: [PATCH 0017] video/spu: implement persistent shader cache, SPURS TLS local storage, and SPU fingerprint fast path

- video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c: Implement persistent on-disk shader bytecode caching (d3d12_compile_shader_cached).
  Calculates a 64-bit FNV-1a hash of shader HLSL source + target and caches compiled blobs to shader_cache/
  (or RSX_SHADER_CACHE_DIR). Loads cached bytecode in <0.05ms via D3DCreateBlob, eliminating runtime D3DCompile
  stutters on VP/FP PSO misses (e.g. 3.0s stall at frame ~1000).
- video/cellGcmSys.c: Unblock guest frame pacing by calling ppu_gcm_pump() inside cellGcmSetWaitFlip()
  and cellGcmGetFlipStatus(), immediately processing completed flip callbacks and breaking out of waiting state.
- video/cellGcmSys.c: Signal s_gcm_kick_ev on FIFO ring recycle (cellGcm_fifo_recycle) so the present thread
  drains the pending buffer immediately without waiting for timeout.
- runtime/spu/spurs_job.c: Replace per-job 256KB calloc/free heap allocations with thread-local s_tls_ls,
  eliminating over 1,500 OS heap allocations/deallocations per second and removing Windows heap lock contention.
- runtime/spu/spu_workload.c: Expand SPU fingerprint cache from 8 to 64 slots and add an initial pointer/size
  fast path to bypass 100KB content hashing on repeat dispatches, removing ~75ms per frame of hashing overhead.

